# Independent adversarial review of dependent-width literal normalization.
#
# The harness drives the real `pycircuit compile` front door once per case in a
# private scratch directory.  It asserts that a matching computed/dependent
# width still binds, that every real width, kind and nominal disagreement is
# still rejected, that an unclosed width never compares equal to a concrete one,
# and - by reading the emitted ac.rule operation - that a rule which binds an
# instance and carries source checks keeps the condition/path suffix positions,
# counts and carrier types.
#
# Defaults on unbound generic definitions do not prove fixed width equality.
# Those two controls are strict negative tests, not xfails or acceptance gaps.
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/literal-normalization-adversarial.py --repo %src --source-compiler %pycircuit_source_unit --linker %pycircuit_link --emitter %pycircuit_emit --scratch %t.dir
